{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgRy9g5RLz8U5oE5cMmPt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01RdEA4q734mrjX8sQwxhgmv","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /private/tmp/h-a6gg20; cat > ANSWER.md <<'EOF'\n# Why the nightly review never reported anything\n\nThe evidence is in `Library/Logs/nightly-review.err`. It holds 6 identical pairs of lines, matching\n`runs = 6` / `last exit code = 1` in `launchctl-print.txt`. So launchd **is** running the job\nevery night. The job just fails before it can tell you.\n\n## Cause 1: the failure path itself crashes (why you never got a failure note)\n\n```\n/Users/vk/bin/nightly-review.zsh:19: read-only variable: status\n```\n\nThe script runs under `/bin/zsh`, and in zsh `status` is a read-only special\nparameter (an alias of `$?`). The line `status=$?` is a fatal error, so the script exits\nwith code 1 right there, before either `notify.sh` call. Success and failure both end\nthe same way: silently. (This would work in bash, which is probably why it looked fine.)\n\n**Fix:** use `rc=$?` instead (`bin/nightly-review.zsh`).\n\n## Cause 2: `claude` isn't authenticated under launchd (why the review fails)\n\n```\nNot logged in · Please run /login\n```\n\nlaunchd doesn't start a login shell and never reads `~/.zshrc`/`~/.zprofile`. Its\nenvironment has only the plist's `PATH` (see `environment = {...}` in the\nlaunchctl output). Whatever authenticates `claude` in your terminal (for example an exported\n`ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`/token in your shell profile) isn't there, so `claude -p` exits\nnon-zero immediately. You can't see that because of Cause 1.\n\n**Fix:** the script now loads a long-lived token from the keychain when none is in the\nenvironment, the same way `notify.sh` gets the Telegram token. If the token is missing, it sends a clear\nfailure note. One-time setup on your Mac:\n\n```sh\nclaude setup-token          # prints a long-lived OAuth token\nsecurity add-generic-password -s claude-nightly-token -a \"$USER\" -w '<token>'\n```\n\n## Problems that would have bitten next (also fixed)\n\n3. **Headless `claude -p` can't approve tool use.** The prompt needs `git log`/`git show`,\n   but in `-p` mode nobody is there to approve a Bash call, so it gets denied and the\n   \"review\" would see no commits. Read-only tools are now pre-approved with\n   `--allowedTools \"Read\" \"Grep\" \"Glob\" \"Bash(git log:*)\" \"Bash(git show:*)\" \"Bash(git diff:*)\"`.\n   Nothing that can write is allowed, so \"Do not modify any file\" is enforced, not just\n   requested.\n4. **Telegram errors were swallowed.** `curl -sS` without `--fail` exits 0 on HTTP\n   400/401, and the response was sent to `/dev/null`. A bad token or a rejected message\n   would look like success. `notify.sh` now uses `--fail-with-body` and prints Telegram's\n   error to stderr, which lands in `nightly-review.err` under launchd.\n5. **The summary could be cut mid-character.** `head -c 300` cuts at byte 300, which can split a\n   multi-byte UTF-8 character, and Telegram rejects invalid UTF-8. The script now sets\n   a UTF-8 locale (launchd sets none) and cuts at 300 *characters* with\n   `${summary[1,300]}`.\n6. Every `notify` call in the script now logs to stderr if `notify.sh` fails, so a broken\n   notifier also leaves a trace in `nightly-review.err`.\n\n## After deploying\n\nCopy `bin/*` back to `~/bin`. The plist didn't need changes, so no reload is required.\nTo test without waiting for 02:30, run `launchctl kickstart gui/$UID/com.vk.nightly-review`,\nthen check Telegram and `~/Library/Logs/nightly-review.err`.\nEOF\ngit status --short"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":937,"cache_read_input_tokens":25474,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":937},"output_tokens":29,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1083ca97-8eff-4772-9574-a882564683cd","uuid":"4c75d72b-2c60-4171-8d25-c9037c9c47f4","timestamp":"2026-10-27T02:40:41.938Z","request_id":"req_011CgRy9foJRxAbg2iJnyjh7","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01RdEA4q734mrjX8sQwxhgmv":{"command":"cd /private/tmp/h-a6gg20; cat > ANSWER.md <<'EOF'\n# Why the nightly review never reported anything\n\nThe evidence is in `Library/Logs/nightly-review.err`. It holds 6 identical pairs of lines, matching\n`runs = 6` / `last exit code = 1` in `launchctl-print.txt`. So launchd **is** running the job\nevery night. The job just fails before it can tell you.\n\n## Cause 1: the failure path itself crashes (why you never got a failure note)\n\n```\n/Users/vk/bin/nightly-review.zsh:19: read-only variable: status\n```\n\nThe script runs under `/bin/zsh`, and in zsh `status` is a read-only special\nparameter (an alias of `$?`). The line `status=$?` is a fatal error, so the script exits\nwith code 1 right there, before either `notify.sh` call. Success and failure both end\nthe same way: silently. (This would work in bash, which is probably why it looked fine.)\n\n**Fix:** use `rc=$?` instead (`bin/nightly-review.zsh`).\n\n## Cause 2: `claude` isn't authenticated under launchd (why the review fails)\n\n```\nNot logged in · Please run /login\n```\n\nlaunchd doesn't start a login shell and never reads `~/.zshrc`/`~/.zprofile`. Its\nenvironment has only the plist's `PATH` (see `environment = {...}` in the\nlaunchctl output). Whatever authenticates `claude` in your terminal (for example an exported\n`ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`/token in your shell profile) isn't there, so `claude -p` exits\nnon-zero immediately. You can't see that because of Cause 1.\n\n**Fix:** the script now loads a long-lived token from the keychain when none is in the\nenvironment, the same way `notify.sh` gets the Telegram token. If the token is missing, it sends a clear\nfailure note. One-time setup on your Mac:\n\n```sh\nclaude setup-token          # prints a long-lived OAuth token\nsecurity add-generic-password -s claude-nightly-token -a \"$USER\" -w '<token>'\n```\n\n## Problems that would have bitten next (also fixed)\n\n3. **Headless `claude -p` can't approve tool use.** The prompt needs `git log`/`git show`,\n   but in `-p` mode nobody is there to approve a Bash call, so it gets denied and the\n   \"review\" would see no commits. Read-only tools are now pre-approved with\n   `--allowedTools \"Read\" \"Grep\" \"Glob\" \"Bash(git log:*)\" \"Bash(git show:*)\" \"Bash(git diff:*)\"`.\n   Nothing that can write is allowed, so \"Do not modify any file\" is enforced, not just\n   requested.\n4. **Telegram errors were swallowed.** `curl -sS` without `--fail` exits 0 on HTTP\n   400/401, and the response was sent to `/dev/null`. A bad token or a rejected message\n   would look like success. `notify.sh` now uses `--fail-with-body` and prints Telegram's\n   error to stderr, which lands in `nightly-review.err` under launchd.\n5. **The summary could be cut mid-character.** `head -c 300` cuts at byte 300, which can split a\n   multi-byte UTF-8 character, and Telegram rejects invalid UTF-8. The script now sets\n   a UTF-8 locale (launchd sets none) and cuts at 300 *characters* with\n   `${summary[1,300]}`.\n6. Every `notify` call in the script now logs to stderr if `notify.sh` fails, so a broken\n   notifier also leaves a trace in `nightly-review.err`.\n\n## After deploying\n\nCopy `bin/*` back to `~/bin`. The plist didn't need changes, so no reload is required.\nTo test without waiting for 02:30, run `launchctl kickstart gui/$UID/com.vk.nightly-review`,\nthen check Telegram and `~/Library/Logs/nightly-review.err`.\nEOF\ngit status --short"}}}
