{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgRyAivbt6gxAkM782nac","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The job has been running every night (6 runs, matching the 6 error pairs in `nightly-review.err`). It fails every time, and the step that should send the failure note crashes first. I wrote the causes up in `ANSWER.md` and fixed both scripts. The changes pass a syntax check, but I haven't run the job: no launchd, keychain or Telegram calls were made.\n\n**The two causes**\n1. **The failure note crashes before it's sent.** In zsh, `status` is a built-in variable you can't assign to. The line `status=$?` kills the script at line 19 with exit code 1, before either `notify.sh` call runs. That's why you got no failure note either. Renamed it to `rc`.\n2. **`claude` isn't logged in when launchd runs it.** launchd doesn't read your shell profile (`~/.zshrc` and friends), so whatever logs `claude` in from your terminal isn't there. The script now reads a long-lived token from the keychain, the same way `notify.sh` gets the Telegram token. If the token is missing, it sends a clear failure message.\n\n**Other problems I fixed, which would have hit you next**\n- In `claude -p` mode nobody is there to approve commands, so every `git log` would have been denied and the review would see no commits. I pre-approved read-only tools only, so \"do not modify any file\" is now enforced rather than just requested.\n- `notify.sh` hid Telegram errors: `curl` exited 0 on a rejected request and the response went to `/dev/null`. It now fails and writes Telegram's error to stderr, which ends up in `nightly-review.err`.\n- `head -c 300` could cut a multi-byte character in half, and Telegram rejects broken UTF-8. The script now sets a UTF-8 locale and truncates at 300 characters instead of bytes.\n\n**What you need to do on your Mac**\n1. Create the token and store it in the keychain (one time):\n   ```sh\n   claude setup-token\n   security add-generic-password -s claude-nightly-token -a \"$USER\" -w '<token>'\n   ```\n2. Copy the two updated scripts from `bin/` back to `~/bin`. The launchd config file didn't change, so it doesn't need reloading.\n3. To test without waiting for 02:30, run `launchctl kickstart gui/$UID/com.vk.nightly-review`, then check Telegram and `~/Library/Logs/nightly-review.err`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1432,"cache_read_input_tokens":26411,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1432},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1083ca97-8eff-4772-9574-a882564683cd","uuid":"0d55c987-ad5f-4286-93ed-656c03ba0cde","timestamp":"2026-10-27T02:40:50.850Z","request_id":"req_011CgRyAigxLDKyJRdgh144w"}
